From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:33:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] ARM: dts: omap3-n950: WL1273 FM radio

The FM part of the N950's WL1273, as Nokia's board-rm680-peripherals.c
wires it: I2C3 address 0x22, interrupt on GPIO 43 (falling edge, as
the driver asks for), reset on GPIO 179. The board file takes GPIO 26
(shared with Bluetooth) only on boards up to revision 0x0324; the N950
at hand reports "RM-680 board, rev 1124" in the boot log of ubiboot's
Harmattan-based kernel, so it has the separate line. The board drives
the line low at start and high to switch the FM part on: active low
as a reset.

The analog output reaches the TWL5031's AUXL and AUXR (Nokia's audio
configuration 4 for the RM-680), already the "FM Radio" input of the
N950's sound card. The board file muxes none of these pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
index d2c7bf8ea..6e3f39f5e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-n950.dts
@@ -553,3 +553,21 @@ gnss@800001fa {
 		host-req-gpios = <&gpio3 31 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;	/* 95 */
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * FM radio: the FM part of the WL1273 at 0x22 on I2C3, its interrupt on
+ * GPIO 43, its reset on GPIO 179, low while off (board-rm680-peripherals.c).
+ * Boards up to revision 0x0324 shared GPIO 26 with Bluetooth instead; the
+ * N950s sold to developers report revision 1124 at boot. The analog output
+ * goes to the TWL5031's AUXL and AUXR inputs, the sound card's "FM Radio"
+ * (Nokia's audio configuration 4 for the RM-680). Nokia's board file sets
+ * no mux for these pins: they stay as the boot loader set them.
+ */
+&i2c3 {
+	fm-radio@22 {
+		compatible = "ti,wl1273-fm";
+		reg = <0x22>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&gpio2 11 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;	/* 43 */
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio6 19 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;			/* 179 */
+	};
+};
